Now the pointermove simplification and rotate-hint removal.

Pointermove handler:
```
canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (event) => {
    if (event.pointerType === 'mouse' || event.buttons || event.pointerType !== 'mouse') handlePointerMove(event);
}, { passive: true });
```
Simply call handlePointerMove. But on touch, pointermove fires while dragging only (touch-action none) — fine. Mouse always. So simplify.

Rotate-hint: remove HTML block, CSS rule, JS dom refs + listener. Also check there's no display logic. `.rotate-hint` display none always. Remove.

